00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.749 align:start position:0%
lost for decades beneath the center of  naples italy the bourbon tunnel is an  underground time capsule of the city's  history  this system of tunnels and caverns was  originally conceived in the 1800s as an  escape tunnel by king ferdinand ii  connecting the royal palace to the  military barracks but the king died  before its completion  the tunnel was then abandoned until the  early 1930s when it was used as a  storage facility for impounded and  contraband vehicles  many of which are still there today  [Music]  during world war ii the tunnel changed  uses again this time becoming a military  hospital and bomb shelter  after the war it turned into a dumping  ground for rubble destroyed cars and  pro-fascist marble statues before it was  sealed and then forgotten  it was accidentally rediscovered in 2005  when government geologists were checking  the conditions of nearby quarries  now the galleria borbonica belongs to  the public who explore the eras before  them as they wander the ancient caverns  [Music]  you
 

